            "notes": "The deck focuses on utilizing powerful graveyard recursive cards and reanimation spells to quickly fill the board with big threats. It aims to overwhelm the opponent with a combination of aggressive creatures and control elements, disrupting their game plan while also presenting a fast clock. Emet-Selch, Unsundered serves as both a powerful reanimation target and a source of card advantage, allowing the deck to maintain pressure and resilience throughout the game. The deck includes a mix of high-impact threats like Griselbrand and Archon of Cruelty, along with disruptive creatures like Opposition Agent and Rune-Scarred Demon. By combining speed, resilience, and disruption, the deck aims to outpace and outmaneuver opponents in a dynamic and aggressive playstyle."
